From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: the shell is told when the foreground window's input language changes (9160)

On Windows ActivateKeyboardLayout tells the shell (HSHELL_LANGUAGE, the
layout in lParam, to WH_SHELL hooks and to the windows registered with
RegisterShellHookWindow) unless KLF_NOTELLSHELL is passed: the input
indicator beside the taskbar clock, and keyboard-indicator programs that
hook the shell, show the layout the foreground window types with. Wine
never sent it, so nothing could follow a switch the person made with the
keyboard (Windows logo key + Space, Left Alt + Shift -- 9154 turns those
into WM_INPUTLANGCHANGEREQUEST and DefWindowProc's activation) or a
program's ActivateKeyboardLayout.

Now NtUserActivateKeyboardLayout calls the WH_SHELL hooks with
HSHELL_LANGUAGE (wParam the foreground window, lParam the layout) and
posts it to the shell hook windows (2207) when the calling thread owns the
foreground window. A thread in the background changes its own layout only:
the indicator does not show it, as on Windows.

Gate test/inputind-gate.sh (with the taskbar's indicator, 9162). Mutant
SG_MUTANT_KBD_NO_TELL_SHELL.
---
 dlls/win32u/input.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -1432,6 +1432,22 @@ static BOOL is_loaded_layout( HKL layout )
     return FALSE;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS (9160): the shell is told the input language changed (HSHELL_LANGUAGE, the layout in
+ * lParam): the input indicator beside the taskbar clock shows the layout the foreground window types with,
+ * whether the person switched it (Windows logo key + Space, Left Alt + Shift, the indicator) or a program
+ * activated one. A thread in the background changes its own layout only, which the indicator does not show. */
+static void tell_shell_language( HKL layout )
+{
+    HWND foreground = NtUserGetForegroundWindow();
+
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_KBD_NO_TELL_SHELL
+    return;
+#endif
+    if (!foreground || get_window_thread( foreground, NULL ) != GetCurrentThreadId()) return;
+    call_hooks( WH_SHELL, HSHELL_LANGUAGE, (WPARAM)foreground, (LPARAM)layout, 0 );
+    shell_hook_notify( HSHELL_LANGUAGE, foreground, (LPARAM)layout );
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *	     NtUserActivateKeyboardLayout    (win32u.@)
  */
@@ -1531,6 +1547,8 @@ HKL WINAPI NtUserActivateKeyboardLayout( HKL layout, UINT flags )
             send_message( focus, WM_INPUTLANGCHANGE, cs.ciCharset, (LPARAM)layout );
     }
 
+    if (!(flags & KLF_NOTELLSHELL)) tell_shell_language( layout );
+
     if (!old_layout) return previous;
     return old_layout;
 }
